{{!
    @template mod_insightjournal/view

    Insight journal activity main view with the prompt and the learner response area.

    The response area has two mutually-exclusive panels, toggled by
    amd/src/autosave.js: a read-only view panel (shown when a saved entry
    exists) and an edit panel containing the rich-text editor (shown
    otherwise, or after clicking Edit). Both panels are always rendered;
    visibility is controlled purely via the "d-none" class so the editor
    only needs to be attached once, at page load.

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * data-cmid
    * data-insightjournal-view
    * data-insightjournal-response-display
    * data-insightjournal-view-status
    * data-insightjournal-edit
    * data-insightjournal-edit-panel
    * data-insightjournal-private
    * data-insightjournal-save
    * data-insightjournal-status
    * data-insightjournal-conflict-banner
    * data-insightjournal-conflict-message
    * data-insightjournal-conflict-content
    * data-insightjournal-conflict-reload

    Note: the response textarea itself has no data attribute. It is rendered
    by entryformhtml (a Moodle moodleform, see classes/form/entry_form.php)
    via core's fixed core_form/editor_textarea template, which does not pass
    through arbitrary attributes, so amd/src/autosave.js locates it by its
    standard Moodle-generated id ("id_response") instead.

    The conflict banner and reload control are rendered server-side too, not
    just toggled by JS: a no-JS POST that hits a save conflict re-renders this
    same template with conflict true, entryformhtml pre-filled with the
    learner's just-submitted draft (never the server's version - the whole
    point is not to silently discard it), and conflictcontent holding the
    server's actual current content alongside it. The reload control is a
    real <a href> to viewurl so it works without JS; autosave.js's own click
    handler (preventDefault + navigating via the link's own href, not
    window.location.reload() - a reload would resubmit the no-JS conflict
    page's POST) still attaches to it unchanged.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * cmid - Course module id.
    * prompt - Pre-formatted prompt HTML (rendered via triple braces).
    * promptstyle - Inline CSS for the prompt box background colour, or '' for none.
    * canwrite - Whether the current user may write a response.
    * haveentry - Whether a saved, non-empty response already exists.
    * entryformhtml - Pre-rendered HTML of the entry_form (response editor, private
      checkbox, save button), or '' when canwrite is false.
    * responseformatted - The user's current response, pre-formatted for display.
    * lastsaved - Localised "last saved" status text.
    * minchars - Minimum characters required, or 0 if none.
    * maxchars - Maximum characters allowed, or 0 for no limit.
    * summaryurl - URL to the personal summary page.
    * canviewall - Whether the user may view the activity report.
    * reporturl - URL to the activity report.
    * sectionurl - URL to the course section where this activity lives.
    * conflict - Whether a no-JS submit just hit a save conflict; forces the edit
      panel open (with the learner's draft) even when haveentry is true.
    * conflictmessage - Localised conflict notice text, or '' when conflict is false.
    * conflictcontent - The server's current content, pre-formatted for display, or
      '' when conflict is false.
    * viewurl - This page's own URL, for the conflict banner's reload link.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "cmid": 5,
        "prompt": "<p>What did you learn today?</p>",
        "promptstyle": "",
        "canwrite": true,
        "haveentry": true,
        "entryformhtml": "<form>...</form>",
        "responseformatted": "<p>Today I learned about Mustache templates.</p>",
        "lastsaved": "Saved 2 minutes ago",
        "minchars": 100,
        "maxchars": 500,
        "summaryurl": "https://example.com/mod/insightjournal/summary.php?courseid=2",
        "canviewall": false,
        "reporturl": "https://example.com/mod/insightjournal/report.php?id=5",
        "sectionurl": "https://example.com/course/view.php?id=2&section=3",
        "conflict": false,
        "conflictmessage": "",
        "conflictcontent": "",
        "viewurl": "https://example.com/mod/insightjournal/view.php?id=5"
    }
}}
<div class="insightjournal-view" data-cmid="{{cmid}}">
    <div class="card mb-3">
        <div class="card-body">
            {{! prompt is pre-sanitised via format_text() in PHP – triple braces intentional, never use for student response }}
            <div class="insightjournal-prompt mb-3"{{#promptstyle}} style="{{promptstyle}}"{{/promptstyle}}>{{{prompt}}}</div>
            {{#canwrite}}
                <div data-insightjournal-view class="{{^haveentry}}d-none {{/haveentry}}{{#conflict}}d-none{{/conflict}}">
                    <div class="insightjournal-response-text mb-2" data-insightjournal-response-display>{{{responseformatted}}}</div>
                    <div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-2">
                        <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" data-insightjournal-edit>{{#str}}edit{{/str}}</button>
                        <span data-insightjournal-view-status class="small text-muted">{{lastsaved}}</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div data-insightjournal-edit-panel class="{{#haveentry}}{{^conflict}}d-none{{/conflict}}{{/haveentry}}">
                    <div class="alert alert-danger {{^conflict}}d-none{{/conflict}}" data-insightjournal-conflict-banner role="alert">
                        <p data-insightjournal-conflict-message class="mb-2">{{conflictmessage}}</p>
                        <div class="insightjournal-conflict-content border rounded p-2 mb-2 bg-white" data-insightjournal-conflict-content>{{{conflictcontent}}}</div>
                        <a href="{{viewurl}}" class="btn btn-danger" data-insightjournal-conflict-reload>{{#str}}conflictreload, mod_insightjournal{{/str}}</a>
                    </div>
                    {{{entryformhtml}}}
                    <div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-2 mt-2">
                        <span data-insightjournal-status role="status" aria-live="polite">{{lastsaved}}</span>
                        {{#maxchars}}<span data-insightjournal-charcounter class="small text-muted ms-auto" aria-live="polite"></span>{{/maxchars}}
                    </div>
                    {{#minchars}}<p id="insightjournal-minchars-note" class="small text-muted mt-2">{{#str}}mincharsnote, mod_insightjournal, {{minchars}}{{/str}}</p>{{/minchars}}
                </div>
            {{/canwrite}}
            {{^canwrite}}
                <div class="alert alert-info">{{#str}}readonlyteacher, mod_insightjournal{{/str}}</div>
            {{/canwrite}}
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-3">
        <a href="{{summaryurl}}" class="btn btn-secondary">{{#str}}mysummary, mod_insightjournal{{/str}}</a>
        {{#canviewall}}<a href="{{reporturl}}" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">{{#str}}report, mod_insightjournal{{/str}}</a>{{/canviewall}}
        <a href="{{sectionurl}}" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">{{#str}}backtosection, mod_insightjournal{{/str}}</a>
    </div>
</div>
